### 21.1 Search quality — done 2026-11-17 — Apify: more about each buyer and supplier
- [x] **(Eng)** The product name sent to the search is a trade name, never the official HS text: on 2026-11-17 cached searches show queries like "Vegetables; onions, whole, cut, sliced, broken or in powder but not… importers, AE". `hs_names.search_name` (curated name → term built from the official text: "dried onions", "turmeric", "frozen shrimp"), used by the picker (shows "searches “…”"), the scan (`search_keyword` replaces an unsearchable name) and `_keyword_for` (never a bare number); curated names added for 0910 / 0909 / 0908 / 0712 / 0703 / 0801 subheadings (turmeric was searched as "spices").
- [x] **(Eng)** Junk results dropped: lead-list pages ("150+ verified buyers", "importers database"), trade-data and promotion sites (IBEF, Eximhub, Megafishnet …); a "buyer" whose own name says Exporters is flagged `role_suspect`; a buyer based outside the searched market is flagged `wrong_market` ("Other country").
- [x] **(Eng)** Search panel: the search name filled in by the picker, a warning when the name reads like the official text, "Will search: … in AE, DE … (catalogue / default markets) · exporters in India · about N paid search lines", the last search's per-market result on the page, results sorted best first. IndiaMART / TradeIndia are no longer called with an empty key (a 403 on every scan).
- [x] **(Eng)** Names: more run-together domains split ("magnafoodservice" → "Magna Food Service"), a leading "Today," / "Hello," dropped.

