### 21.3 More buyers and suppliers to choose from — new list actors — Apify: more about each buyer and supplier
Today buyers and suppliers come from one source: a web search per product × market (`company-contact-finder-ai`), about 5 companies a line. These actors add lists that are larger and better qualified. All are PortLess's own actors (`/actor-pipeline`, the `rich_minds` plan cannot run Store actors), read public pages only (respect each site's terms and robots rules; no LinkedIn scraping), and feed the same path: rows → `quality.py` / `validation.py` → directory with `source` → radar, desk and score. Each row keeps where it came from, so 18.1 "how each opportunity was found" can compare sources by deals won.

Suppliers (India) — authoritative lists first:
- [ ] **(Eng) P1** **Indian exporter registries** — `india-exporter-registries-ai`: the public registered-exporter lists of the Spices Board (CRES), APEDA, MPEDA (seafood), Tea / Coffee Boards and FIEO's member directory: company, registration number, products, city / state, contact. Registered exporters of the exact product, with a number the check can verify (13.6 checks a known supplier; this finds them).
- [ ] **(Eng) P1** **Indian B2B supplier listings** — `india-b2b-suppliers-ai` (the `india-supplier-finder-ai` slot that was never built): public seller pages of IndiaMART, TradeIndia and ExportersIndia per product: company, city, listed price and unit, MOQ, GST-verified badge, years in business. Gives prices for the radar's supplier side before any RFQ. Works without the paid IndiaMART API keys.
- [ ] **(Eng) P2** **Mandi traders** — licensed commission agents / traders published by state agricultural marketing boards (APMC) for the commodity's main mandis: sourcing for raw agri goods (onion, chilli, turmeric) beyond exporters.

Buyers (importers abroad):
- [ ] **(Eng) P1** **Association member lists** — `trade-association-members-ai`: member directories of ASTA (US spices), European Spice Association and its national members, FEDIOL, national rice / seafood / nut federations, Gulf foodstuff traders' groups. Members are established importers of the exact product. (The search drops association sites as "not a company" — right for the site itself; their member lists are the value.)
- [ ] **(Eng) P1** **Names out of "top importers" pages** — `importer-list-extractor-ai`: the "Top 20 spice importers in Germany" / "rice importers in Dubai" articles the search drops today are lists of real companies. Extract the named companies from those pages, then run the contact finder on each — turns the junk the search finds into leads.
- [ ] **(Eng) P1** **Business directories with categories** — `b2b-directory-companies-ai`: free public listings of Europages, Kompass (free tier), Dubai Chamber / Saudi chambers' member search, German IHK company search, by activity code and country: company, activity, size class, website. Many importers that do not rank in a web search.
- [ ] **(Eng) P1** **Local business listings** — `local-business-leads-ai` on the Google Places API (needs a Google Maps Platform key, paid per request — cheaper than a Store actor and allowed by Google's terms): "spice wholesaler Hamburg", "rice trader Deira": name, address, phone, website, rating. Strong for wholesale markets (Dubai, Hamburg, Rotterdam, New Jersey).
- [ ] **(Eng) P2** **Public buy requests** — `buy-leads-ai`: buy-offer boards (go4WorldBusiness, TradeKey, ExportersIndia buy leads, Alibaba RFQ public pages): buyer country, product, quantity, date. Real demand signals for 18.1 "demand signals create opportunities"; many are brokers, so they go through the same checks and start as `unverified`.
- [ ] **(Eng) P2** **Food procurement tenders** beyond EU TED — `food-tenders-ai`: UN Global Marketplace (UNGM), World Food Programme, Saudi Etimad, US SAM.gov food awards: buyer, product, quantity, deadline. Large, paid-on-time buyers; a tender is time-boxed (urgency tier 3).
- [ ] **(Eng) P2** **Who buys from the competing origins** — `competitor-clients-ai`: the "our clients / where we export" pages of the leading exporters from the market's main competing origin (from the radar's `competitors`, e.g. Vietnamese pepper exporters): named importers already buying the product from someone else — the buyers India's price advantage (16) is pitched to.

Both:
- [ ] **(Eng) P1** **Trade-fair exhibitors** — already 21.2 (`trade-fair-exhibitors-ai`); add the Indian fairs (World Food India, AAHAR, India International Seafood Show, Spices fairs) for suppliers.
- [ ] **(Eng)** **One de-duplication across sources** — the same company from three lists becomes one directory record (domain → registration number → name + city), with every source kept in `sources`; a company found by more sources scores higher (it is more likely real and active).
- [ ] **(Eng)** **Per-source yield on the radar / directory** — companies found, verified, contacted, replied, quoted and traded per source and per Apify dollar, so the next actor money goes to the source that turns into deals.
- [ ] **(Legal)** Confirm per source that reading and storing the listing is allowed (site terms, database rights in the EU) and that the outreach rules of 20 (cold e-mail per market) apply to every list.


