- [ ] **P0** Legal form of the company (private limited, LLP or proprietorship) and the state of the registered office — every registration depends on it (14.1). **Recommendation:** private limited.
- [ ] **P0** Which AD Category-I bank (forex desk, export credit, EDPMS support, charges) (14.3).
- [ ] **P1** Which products to register for first (decides the RCMC: Spices Board, APEDA, FIEO) (14.2).

## Done in the latest rounds (for reference)

- Full-flow journey TC-E2E-000 / UC-15 on every simulator; `@journey:` link between Gherkin and journeys.
- Fixed: RFQ to scan-found suppliers, SDF / Shipping Bill on CIF deals, nameless e-mailed quotes, QIMA booking without a supplier address, Tazapay proof links in automation.
- Supplier facility address asked, read from e-mails and required before the inspection (`QC_FACILITY_ADDRESS_REQUIRED`).
- Prices to Indian suppliers in INR with the USD contract price and rate; quotations mirrored in their own currency.
- Confirming a match closes the deal's other proposals.
- Buyer / supplier check at scan time (12): the top buyers and suppliers of every opportunity are screened (sanctions, e-mail, GST / IEC) before the radar shows them; the radar shows verified ones by default ("Verified only / All" toggle, hidden counts), the directory filters by result and can check one company now, a failed counterparty never seeds outreach or a supplier party, and a deal from an opportunity no longer records an unchecked supplier as verified.
- Pre-deal rescore (12): the radar's Rescore / Start prospect fills the best pairs' gaps without contacting anyone (counterparty check, supplier address / GSTIN from its website, plant-to-port distance, an estimated supplier price labelled as an estimate), scores them again and shows before → after; a web-search buyer's product fit is no longer overstated as "same subheading".
- Readiness check `counterparty_validation` (12): fails in production (warns elsewhere) when `TRADE_MIN_VALIDATION_ENABLED=false` or the screening actor has no `APIFY_TOKEN`, so the radar's "Verified only" view can no longer be silently empty.
- Opportunity Radar ranked by expected profit (16): margin per MT / container / lot, chance of closing (pair score, verified buyers, outcome calibration, corridor history), each price with its basis (buyer quote → price book → India-to-market → market average; supplier price → price book → Agmarknet mandi → India export average); net gap = gross − duty − freight (VAT no longer subtracted); implausible gaps flagged; Indian exporters listed as buyers and suppliers of another product flagged; cleaner company names; chilli / turmeric / saffron keywords fixed; scan report with drop reasons; running-deal warning; outreach names India's price advantage when Comtrade shows it.
- Unit test cases in Gherkin per module (`docs/testing/unit/`, `scripts/gen_unit_gherkin.py`).
- Buyers & Suppliers card view and company profile (20): pipeline strip, new this week, hot companies, side panel with next moves / prospects / timeline, add to prospect.
- Buyer / seller search quality (21.1): searchable trade names instead of the official HS text, junk pages dropped, exporter and other-country buyers flagged, search panel shows what it will search and the last result, IndiaMART / TradeIndia not called without keys.
- Buyers & Suppliers as a trading book (20): relationship stage, activity, prices and score per company; do-not-contact list honoured across prospects; exporter "buyers" skipped; directory names and roles cleaned.
- Prospect desk (19): worth / whose move / next moves per prospect, walk-away and target prices, quote age and leverage, one cost model with the radar; outreach no longer opens with the contact finder's operator note, failed sends are recorded, only booked inspectors are named.
- Opportunity Radar hand-off and truer profit (16): ready-to-start checklist, radar estimate carried into the deal and compared with the realised margin, export policy / news / destination needs before a deal, data year, export incentives, freight per lane, container per product, profit range, live USD/INR and mandi trend, yearly potential, scan cost, "what's missing and where to get it", time-sensitive sort, origin opportunity on the deal page.
- PI acceptance price check (5.1, DEF-12 / TC-RSK-024): a buyer e-mail that accepts the PI but names another price (unit or total, rupees converted) opens `CONFIRM_PI_ACCEPTANCE` at L0 with flag `pi_price_mismatch` and both prices in the summary; repeating the PI price or total, or naming none, stays a plain acceptance.

